t $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nTo create a schematic of the Cartesian product, we create a table and list the elements of the first set $A$ in a row across the top and the elements of the second set $B$ in a column down the left side.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/assets/8fe661f4daa7a5bb75dea993f46bbf8970400a798e23da4018d3e4a0b891273d.png)\n\nThen, at each intersection, we write an ordered pair whose first coordinate is the corresponding element of $A$ and the second coordinate is the corresponding element of $B.$\n\nOur completed $A\\times B$ schematic is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/assets/49270545404b21e8068b35cdb59c756e1f3bc3c22608359c8d7e83389e38c7a4.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186307285 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b304527c-5cdc-57df-b118-e555f6f8fa5c" :knowledge-point/title "Creating a Schematic for a Cartesian Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "710c12de-5d01-5b08-bbc9-ef2f623d067e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307287} {:answer/id #uuid "788ab1c9-a77b-5ebe-9ea8-c085ff8a685f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307288} {:answer/id #uuid "b8255dae-9506-5229-829b-b36f76b3e4e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307289} {:answer/id #uuid "6519ab84-a21e-5fcd-a8e6-ab23a33f8df0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307290} {:answer/id #uuid "97963324-1fd9-5c84-9ade-883794dce552" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307291}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "710c12de-5d01-5b08-bbc9-ef2f623d067e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307287} :answer-field/id #uuid "f33d4708-7849-502c-b078-0d0aa6a56353" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307286}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5132636e-fc5c-596d-8624-67ad2af0f5ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-181963" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/assets/cb3e6ef6a832f2adbbc5e096bddf2c4f6a0445fbd77a71df5617298f8dad2e51.png)\n\nBy finding the missing entries in the schematic shown above for $A\\times B,$ where $A={a,b,c}$ and $B={2,4,6},$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\n- $(4,b)\\in A\\times B$\n- $(c,6)\\in A\\times B$\n- $(a,2)\\in A\\times B$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nTo complete our schematic of $A\\times B,$ we write an ordered pair whose first coordinate is the corresponding element of $A$ and the second coordinate is the corresponding element of $B$ at each intersection.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/assets/57d053cca53046f02201540e655030a37ba8f7a2811e7dc724cf30ca9fd3c072.png)\n\nAccording to our diagram:\n\n- $(4,b)\\notin A\\times B\\,\\times $\n\n- $(c,6)\\in A\\times B\\,✓$\n\n- $(a,2)\\in A\\times B\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186307292 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3fca5176-1359-5ad8-b012-592ffa9b20b5" :knowledge-point/title "Cartesian Products With Three Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d7aadcf-3f0c-5f06-b72f-7ff02cd37583" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307294} {:answer/id #uuid "4d2398c0-c051-5422-82f4-f308f6b14470" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307295} {:answer/id #uuid "ce44dfa5-985d-532f-aa9f-556b6804087b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307296} {:answer/id #uuid "98de2af1-6c6d-5db7-ac9d-752cb3fc604f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307297} {:answer/id #uuid "c42dbbae-263f-5b39-b543-214afeffae62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307298}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d2398c0-c051-5422-82f4-f308f6b14470" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307295} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5c27ca0-cc9f-5eeb-a0c7-07394a59600e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307293}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3712bfaa-78a9-5a17-a771-28da720170a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-181969" :question/problem "If $A={p,q,r}$ and $B={3,5},$ which of the following elements belong to $B\\times (A\\times A)?$\n\n- $(5,(r,p))$\n- $(q,(5,3))$\n- $(3,q,p)$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nIn this case, $A\\times A$ consists of every combination of ${p,q,r}$ with ${p,q,r},$ as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/assets/aad91ef7655fa8a5bf0c9852ee4e5e2166289087a56ac18e932ee3cce17164a0.png)\n\nHence, the set $A\\times A$ is given by\n\n$$\nA\\times A={(p,p),(p,q),(p,r),(q,p),(q,q),(q,r),(r,p),(r,q),(r,r)}.\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n|A\\times A|=|A|\\cdot |A|=3\\cdot 3=9.\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian product\n\n$$\nB\\times (A\\times A)\n$$\n\nconsists of every combination of $B$ and $A\\times A,$ as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/assets/e573cecaa9333e071d980b1b03d65dafadd027506d2c2b9b6e8acfbe15d3be52.png)\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n|B\\times (A\\times A)|=|B|\\cdot |A\\times A|=2\\cdot 9=18.\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, we see that only $(5,(r,p))\\in B\\times (A\\times A).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186307299 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3fca5176-1359-5ad8-b012-592ffa9b20b5" :knowledge-point/title "Cartesian Products With Three Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "167bd4a0-eb39-581e-bfa8-929daf19cd91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307301} {:answer/id #uuid "c97928e8-88e3-5bd9-8bba-c39545fb1a3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307302} {:answer/id #uuid "40510ba4-21d8-5958-a99f-d6df4d4cbdb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307303} {:answer/id #uuid "6640ff23-c438-594c-9431-97f3c2dd86f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307304} {:answer/id #uuid "2a87810d-b698-58e1-9820-3c7faffdd0a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307305}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6640ff23-c438-594c-9431-97f3c2dd86f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307304} :answer-field/id #uuid "1dc42bf0-d9ae-511b-98de-edb25515c718" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307300}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4532b14e-91fc-5f93-8767-7d104cf33cfc" :question/math-academy-id "q-181977" :question/problem "If $A={4,8}$ and $B={x,y,z},$ which of the following elements belong to $A\\times (A\\times B)?$\n\n- $(4,(8,z))$\n- $(8,(8,x))$\n- $(8,4,y)$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nIn this case, $A\\times B$ consists of every combination of ${4,8}$ with ${x,y,z},$ as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/assets/72feee192b949dcce7b0f10f4e1d772c809bcf73de6c66f15c7de75a4a1ff672.png)\n\nHence, the set $A\\times B$ is given by\n\n$$\nA\\times B={(4,x),(4,y),(4,z),(8,x),(8,y),(8,z)}.\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n|A\\times B|=|A|\\cdot |B|=2\\cdot 3=6.\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian product\n\n$$\nA\\times (A\\times B)\n$$\n\nconsists of every combination of $A$ and $A\\times B,$ as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/assets/1ae41857d4aee82a2a4ad838c20bbe72b05a1505a5f4df3aa4a86fda0fff0612.png)\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n|A\\times (A\\times B)|=|A|\\cdot |A\\times B|=2\\cdot 6=12.\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, we see that both $(4,(8,z))$ and $(8,(8,x))$ are in $A\\times \\text{\\(}A\\times B).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186307306 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6128eca-7f76-5386-9d67-d81db2943eeb" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Cartesian Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0119a112-a132-5a23-bd6e-d38630fa400b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307308} {:answer/id #uuid "7cbabf2f-dba4-55aa-a558-3542bd4a8d1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307309} {:answer/id #uuid "092019fb-1a1f-5daf-a555-1670b49327d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307310} {:answer/id #uuid "f8ca8275-6f04-56b7-98c8-c185be48f242" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307311} {:answer/id #uuid "0bd80223-893d-5c56-9598-51ccd83e8539" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307312}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7cbabf2f-dba4-55aa-a558-3542bd4a8d1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307309} :answer-field/id #uuid "9507f8e2-762f-53d5-94c4-e4d50ed3352b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307307}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f5d7f61b-30af-5356-9974-c82d04c8d403" :question/math-academy-id "q-182015" :question/problem "For the sets $X={5,10},$ $Y={r,s,t},$ and $Z=X\\times Y,$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\n- $(5,r)\\in Z$\n- $(r,t)\\in Z$\n- $(10,s)\\in Z$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $X\\times Y$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $X$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $Y.$\n\nIn this case, the schematic for $X\\times Y$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/assets/1eb13d93fbefc4c7285edef537a9fb3e21339f7a3b37a179eeb150db8d726c1b.png)\n\nHence, the set $Z=X\\times Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nZ={(5,r),(5,s),(5,t),(10,r),(10,s),(10,t)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186307313 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6128eca-7f76-5386-9d67-d81db2943eeb" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Cartesian Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ae0b1c1-a021-56d6-b313-346e8d0cb38b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307315} {:answer/id #uuid "cb6ddf35-4b3e-58cf-8a3b-9552489e6d70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307316} {:answer/id #uuid "39925016-5352-5852-a55a-0b26479919e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307317} {:answer/id #uuid "d977a360-4135-592f-8690-55291e78e071" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307318} {:answer/id #uuid "61352dc0-8a99-542f-972c-39acfed44229" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307319}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb6ddf35-4b3e-58cf-8a3b-9552489e6d70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307316} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f890219-b9ca-5354-ab79-31d6d5342ad4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307314}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "46026c28-5034-5311-8d1e-61a2b4c96055" :question/math-academy-id "q-182018" :question/problem "For the sets $X={f,g,h}$ and $Z=X\\times X,$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\n- $(f,g)\\in Z$\n- $(f,g,h)\\in Z$\n- $(h,h)\\in Z$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $X\\times X$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $X$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $X.$\n\nIn this case, the schematic for ${X}^{2}=X\\times X$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/assets/1718bd6f3f2eaa8dd8fe581b0d938b3b5f1928d5e56a11a324f145e7a481fabe.png)\n\nHence, the set $Z=X\\times X$ is given by\n\n$$\nZ={(f,f),(f,g),(f,h),(g,f),(g,g),(g,h),(h,f),(h,g),(h,h)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186307320 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6128eca-7f76-5386-9d67-d81db2943eeb" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Cartesian Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "121905aa-94fa-5d2c-aaca-ea7694b1eda7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307322} {:answer/id #uuid "ce4e5497-b854-5f34-ba7c-4c4b64101120" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307323} {:answer/id #uuid "6e09c20f-6133-5dba-8a0b-2fc60c851904" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307324} {:answer/id #uuid "9640a8fe-d4d7-5b1e-b59c-10b687306d2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307325} {:answer/id #uuid "a8fa33ad-09e0-5d8f-992a-326e5fe18294" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307326}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e09c20f-6133-5dba-8a0b-2fc60c851904" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307324} :answer-field/id #uuid "730ccd69-10ad-5abf-b1ab-0f1d4ff5b6db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307321}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4ac32124-0bcf-5c97-9daa-ea223712f992" :question/math-academy-id "q-182021" :question/problem "For the sets $X={k,m,n}$ and $Z=X\\times X,$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\n- ${k}^{2}\\in Z$\n- $(k,n,m)\\in Z$\n- $(m,n)\\in Z$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $X\\times X$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $X$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $X.$\n\nIn this case, the schematic for ${X}^{2}=X\\times X$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/assets/e7c24108e0d9f5e2e7edbfbe90cdf7318bc247aa73a4c9c72dc61449c7b4da94.png)\n\nHence, the set $Z=X\\times X$ is given by\n\n$$\nZ={(k,k),(k,m),(k,n),(m,k),(m,m),(m,n),(n,k),(n,m),(n,n)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186307327 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "88fb08f1-03f1-5b04-8b48-4b153e522040" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Cardinality of a Cartesian Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "045924ed-62ea-58a4-b6df-17ab9936a70c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307329} {:answer/id #uuid "8f8f883c-8b57-556c-aab7-0db9175c0380" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307330} {:answer/id #uuid "8ddde432-c31c-5401-850b-9055f8db9024" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307331} {:answer/id #uuid "c1612323-c283-5b05-972f-78e82733571a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307332} {:answer/id #uuid "5e88f8f2-e46f-5978-b2a1-781dbe8dd9c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307333}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1612323-c283-5b05-972f-78e82733571a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307332} :answer-field/id #uuid "f784a3d9-c021-595d-a654-bc10f850ff91" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307328}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f4ca1546-8f70-5dcb-a76f-07fccccb8754" :question/math-academy-id "q-80442" :question/problem "What is the cardinality of $A\\times B$ for $A={0,1,2,3,...,7}$ and $B={a,b,c,d}?$" :question/worked-solution "For any two finite sets $A$ and $B,$ the cardinality of $A\\times B$ is\n\n$$\n|A\\times B|=|A|\\cdot |B|.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A\\times B| & =|A|\\cdot |B| \\\\  & =8\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186307334 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "88fb08f1-03f1-5b04-8b48-4b153e522040" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Cardinality of a Cartesian Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "438a3be3-4a65-5dc9-90a0-c9c1d8460b9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307336} {:answer/id #uuid "5f8dcab1-ee34-52e1-9d09-46f917c420b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307337} {:answer/id #uuid "3ce3adfa-bc33-5be1-8373-980411a18ebd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307338} {:answer/id #uuid "b3e19e84-6480-568a-97c7-8ab8b12c3c4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307339} {:answer/id #uuid "371a85d8-2f9f-5363-8d36-03dcdd630aff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307340}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "371a85d8-2f9f-5363-8d36-03dcdd630aff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307340} :answer-field/id #uuid "d61530d5-0664-50cd-858f-7fa2c394ed4f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307335}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "72bc95df-feed-5067-9554-2728f0326b02" :question/math-academy-id "q-80894" :question/problem "What is the cardinality of $H\\times K$ for $H={1,2,3,…,9}$ and $K={x,y}?$" :question/worked-solution "For any two finite sets $H$ and $K,$ the cardinality of $H\\times K$ is\n\n$$\n|H\\times K|=|H|\\cdot |K|.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|H\\times K| & =|H|\\cdot |K| \\\\  & =9\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186307341 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "88fb08f1-03f1-5b04-8b48-4b153e522040" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Cardinality of a Cartesian Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f1aaeed2-fef2-58f9-800a-30b7bbcb98d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307343} {:answer/id #uuid "50c8a700-1846-5081-b169-b4165898d8b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307344} {:answer/id #uuid "caeeb93e-9314-594c-ab6d-fefe6bf9fa2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307345} {:answer/id #uuid "59ed3f73-2c7c-5e5e-8c4a-33660cb2b0af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307346} {:answer/id #uuid "ba3c3d7a-c431-51b5-825e-9233ade48334" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307347}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba3c3d7a-c431-51b5-825e-9233ade48334" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307347} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3362ecc-966f-5374-85f5-296fe8f4ca31" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307342}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "388a46c3-a211-5754-ba5c-bd7e7769886d" :question/math-academy-id "q-80896" :question/problem "What is the cardinality of $C\\times D$ for $C={0,1,2,...,11}$ and $D={s,t,u,v}?$" :question/worked-solution "For any two finite sets $C$ and $D,$ the cardinality of $C\\times D$ is\n\n$$\n|C\\times D|=|C|\\cdot |D|.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|C\\times D| & =|C|\\cdot |D| \\\\  & =12\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =48.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
